      "title": "Implementing the UNESCO Recommendation on the Ethics of AI",
      "order": 5,
      "organizer": "UNESCO IFAP's Information Ethics Working Group (IEWG)",
      "slug": "implementing-the-unesco-recommendation-on-the-ethics-of-ai",
      "description": "Inspired by the Universal Declaration of Human Rights, UNESCO IFAP’s Information Ethics Working Group (IEWG) studies the ethical, legal and social aspects of the applications of ICT. The group brings together a diverse set of experts from different sectors around the world to tackle some of the most pressing issues in this field. \n\nAs artificial intelligence (AI) technologies have gained traction in virtually every aspect of our lives, ethics of AI too have become increasingly more important. In 2020, UNESCO brought together an ad hoc group of experts to craft a Recommendation on the ethics of AI, which has since been adopted. The IEWG has now turned its expertise to this global standard setting document, focusing on how it can be implemented in the ecosystem. In collaboration with international research centers and other UNESCO programs, including the Global AI Ethics Consortium, the Global AI Ethics Network for Social Good, the Global Network on AI and International Society and the Information Ethics Network for Africa, the IEWG has developed this series to help AI ethics practitioners implement the Recommendation in practice. \n\nTo learn more about the IEWG’s work, please visit: www.crids.eu/cooperations/iewg-ifap. "
    }
